 market.\nL3252@P118: Modifications to costs can be made in the ‘Dashboard,’ ‘Chem,’ and ‘Cost Input’ worksheets.\nL3253@P118: 9.2.1 Battery Specific Materials Costs\nL3254@P118: The default costs of the main battery materials are provided in Table 9.1. These values are included\nL3741@P128: contamination. These steps include electrode slitting, cell stacking, current collector welding, X\u0002ray inspection, insertion of cell into a container, and electrolyte filling. BatPaC v5.0 provides labor\nL3742@P128: and capital equipment costs for all these steps. The area is provided as a lump sum for all steps in\nL3743@P128: the dry room.\nL3744@P128: 9.3.2.1 Electrode Slitting\nL3745@P128: Upon entering the dry room, the electrode foils are first slit into individual electrodes. The values\nL4089@P136: everything scales with production rate (no utilization). Options can be selected in ‘Dashboard’ and\nL4090@P136: should not be modified in ‘Manufacturing Cost’ worksheet (note description of purple cells in\nL4091@P136: Section 3.2.1 indicates they should not be modified).\nL4092@P136: 9.6 Unit Costs for Battery Pack\nL4093@P136: The unit costs of the battery pack are calculated as summarized in Table 9.10. The total cost is the\nL4094@P136: combination of variable costs, fixed expenses, profits, and warranty. Default assumptions for these\n"
